{"ID":83,"post_author":"1","post_date":"2026-03-05 17:37:00","post_date_gmt":"2026-03-05 17:37:00","post_content":"<p><img width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/Aadiguru1staacharya.jpg\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/Aadiguru1staacharya.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/Aadiguru1staacharya-300x300.jpg 300w, https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/Aadiguru1staacharya-150x150.jpg 150w, https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/Aadiguru1staacharya-768x768.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<!DOCTYPE html><br \/>\n<html lang=\"en\"><br \/>\n<head><br \/>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><br \/>\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"><br \/>\n    <title>Jagadguru Adi Shankaracharya | Shivbodh Trust<\/title><br \/>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Biography of Jagadguru Adi Shankaracharya, the proponent of Advaita Vedanta and founder of the four Amnaya Peethams.\"><br \/>\n    <!-- Fonts & Icons -->\n    <link href=\"https:\/\/cdnjs.cloudflare.com\/ajax\/libs\/font-awesome\/6.4.0\/css\/all.min.css\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n    <link href=\"https:\/\/fonts.googleapis.com\/css2?family=Alegreya:wght@400;700&family=Cinzel:wght@500;700;800;900&family=Rozha+One&family=Poppins:wght@300;400;600&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n    <!-- CSS Link -->\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n<\/head><br \/>\n<body><br \/>\n    <!-- TOP NAVIGATION --><\/p>\n<header>\n        <a href=\"#\"><br \/>\n             Shivbodh Trust<br \/>\n        <\/a><br \/>\n            Vishwaas se Shivbodh<br \/>\n    <\/header>\n<p>    <!-- NEW UPDATED TICKER --><br \/>\n                    \ud83d\udc04<br \/>\n                        <strong>Go Matdata Abhiyan<\/strong> | Give a missed call to join: 844 853 1008<br \/>\n            <!-- Duplicate for infinite scroll --><br \/>\n                    \ud83d\udc04<br \/>\n                        <strong>Go Matdata Abhiyan<\/strong> | Give a missed call to join: 844 853 1008<br \/>\n            <!-- Extra Duplicate for smooth continuous scroll if needed --><br \/>\n                    \ud83d\udc04<br \/>\n                        <strong>Go Matdata Abhiyan<\/strong> | Give a missed call to join: 844 853 1008<br \/>\n    <!-- GRAND HERO SECTION --><\/p>\n<header>\n            <!-- Updated Sanskrit Sloka --><br \/>\n            \u0965 \u0950 \u0917\u0941\u0930\u0935\u0947 \u0928\u092e\u0903 \u0965<br \/>\n            <!-- Highlighted Hero Title --><\/p>\n<h1 style=\"font-size: 4rem; color: #FFD700; text-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9), 0 0 20px #FFD700; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-bottom: 10px;\">Jagadguru Adi Shankaracharya<\/h1>\n<p>            The Eternal Reviver of Sanatana Dharma<br \/>\n    <\/header>\n<p>    <!-- CONTENT SECTION --><\/p>\n<article>\n<h2 style=\"font-size: 2.5rem; color: #D4AF37; font-family: 'Cinzel', serif;\">The Divine Incarnation<\/h2>\n<p>                    <strong>\u0906\u0926\u093f \u0936\u0902\u0915\u0930\u093e\u091a\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f (Adi Shankaracharya)<\/strong> \u2013 \u0938\u0928\u093e\u0924\u0928 \u0927\u0930\u094d\u092e \u0915\u0947 \u092e\u0939\u093e\u0928\u0924\u092e \u0926\u093e\u0930\u094d\u0936\u0928\u093f\u0915 \u0914\u0930 \u0905\u0926\u094d\u0935\u0948\u0924 \u0935\u0947\u0926\u093e\u0902\u0924 (Advaita Vedanta) \u0915\u0947 \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0923\u0947\u0924\u093e \u0925\u0947\u0964 \u0909\u0928\u0915\u093e \u091c\u0928\u094d\u092e \u0915\u0947\u0930\u0932 \u0915\u0947 \u0915\u093e\u0932\u0921\u0940 (Kalady) \u0917\u093e\u0902\u0935 \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0936\u093f\u0935\u0917\u0941\u0930\u0941 \u0914\u0930 \u0906\u0930\u094d\u092f\u093e\u092e\u094d\u092c\u093e \u0915\u0947 \u0918\u0930 \u0939\u0941\u0906 \u0925\u093e\u0964 \u0909\u0928\u094d\u0939\u094b\u0902\u0928\u0947 \u092c\u093e\u0932\u094d\u092f\u0915\u093e\u0932 \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0939\u0940 \u0935\u0947\u0926\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u093e \u0905\u0927\u094d\u092f\u092f\u0928 \u092a\u0942\u0930\u094d\u0923 \u0915\u0930 \u0932\u093f\u092f\u093e \u0925\u093e \u0914\u0930 \u0905\u092a\u0928\u0947 \u0917\u0941\u0930\u0941 \u0917\u094b\u0935\u093f\u0902\u0926 \u092d\u0917\u0935\u0924\u094d\u092a\u093e\u0926 (Govinda Bhagavatpada) \u0938\u0947 \u091c\u094d\u091e\u093e\u0928 \u092a\u094d\u0930\u093e\u092a\u094d\u0924 \u0915\u0930 \u0938\u0902\u092a\u0942\u0930\u094d\u0923 \u092d\u093e\u0930\u0924\u0935\u0930\u094d\u0937 \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0905\u0926\u094d\u0935\u0948\u0924 \u0926\u0930\u094d\u0936\u0928 \u0915\u093e \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0938\u093e\u0930 \u0915\u093f\u092f\u093e\u0964<\/p>\n<p style=\"font-size:1.15rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #444; text-align: justify;\">\n                    Jagadguru Adi Shankaracharya was a profound Indian philosopher, Vedic scholar, and the foremost proponent of the Advaita Vedanta (Non-Dualism) doctrine. Born in Kalady, Kerala to a Brahmin family (Sivaguru and Aryamba), he displayed extraordinary intellect from a very young age. Leaving home early in his life, he traveled to the banks of the Narmada River to become a disciple of Guru Govinda Bhagavatpada, under whose compassionate guidance he mastered all Vedic scriptures. In his brief life, he composed brilliant commentaries (Bhashyas) on the Upanishads, the Brahma Sutras, and the Bhagavad Gita, systematically unifying the diverse sects of Hinduism and revitalizing Sanatana Dharma across the Indian subcontinent.\n                <\/p>\n<h3 style=\"font-family:'Cinzel',serif; color:#D35400; margin-bottom:20px; font-size:2rem; font-weight:800;\">Establishment of the Four Amnaya Peethams<\/h3>\n<p style=\"font-size:1.15rem; margin-bottom:25px; line-height: 1.8; color: #444;\">\n                    To preserve and propagate the essence of Sanatana Dharma and the Vedas for eternity, Adi Shankaracharya established four cardinal monastic institutions known as <strong>Amnaya Peethams<\/strong> in the four corners of India. He appointed his four prime ascetic disciples as the heads of these centers, each entrusted with the safeguarding of one specific Veda. This ensured the unbroken continuity of the Guru-Shishya Parampara (lineage) that thrives to this very day.\n                <\/p>\n<p>                    \u0938\u0928\u093e\u0924\u0928 \u0927\u0930\u094d\u092e \u0914\u0930 \u0935\u0947\u0926\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u0940 \u0936\u093e\u0936\u094d\u0935\u0924 \u0930\u0915\u094d\u0937\u093e \u0915\u0947 \u0932\u093f\u090f, \u0909\u0928\u094d\u0939\u094b\u0902\u0928\u0947 \u092d\u093e\u0930\u0924 \u0915\u0940 \u091a\u093e\u0930\u094b\u0902 \u0926\u093f\u0936\u093e\u0913\u0902 \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u091a\u093e\u0930 \u092a\u094d\u0930\u092e\u0941\u0916 \u092e\u0920\u094b\u0902 (\u0906\u092e\u094d\u0928\u093e\u092f \u092a\u0940\u0920\u094b\u0902) \u0915\u0940 \u0938\u094d\u0925\u093e\u092a\u0928\u093e \u0915\u0940 \u2013 <strong>\u0917\u094b\u0935\u0930\u094d\u0927\u0928 \u092e\u0920 (\u092a\u0941\u0930\u0940)<\/strong> \u092a\u0942\u0930\u094d\u0935 \u092e\u0947\u0902, <strong>\u0936\u093e\u0930\u0926\u093e \u092a\u0940\u0920 (\u0936\u094d\u0930\u0943\u0902\u0917\u0947\u0930\u0940)<\/strong> \u0926\u0915\u094d\u0937\u093f\u0923 \u092e\u0947\u0902, <strong>\u0936\u093e\u0930\u0926\u093e \u092a\u0940\u0920 (\u0926\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0930\u0915\u093e)<\/strong> \u092a\u0936\u094d\u091a\u093f\u092e \u092e\u0947\u0902, \u0914\u0930 <strong>\u091c\u094d\u092f\u094b\u0924\u093f\u0930\u094d\u092e\u0920 (\u092c\u0926\u094d\u0930\u0940\u0928\u093e\u0925)<\/strong> \u0909\u0924\u094d\u0924\u0930 \u092e\u0947\u0902\u0964 \u092f\u0947 \u092e\u0920 \u0915\u094d\u0930\u092e\u0936\u0903 \u090b\u0917\u094d\u0935\u0947\u0926, \u092f\u091c\u0941\u0930\u094d\u0935\u0947\u0926, \u0938\u093e\u092e\u0935\u0947\u0926 \u0914\u0930 \u0905\u0925\u0930\u094d\u0935\u0935\u0947\u0926 \u0915\u0940 \u091c\u094d\u091e\u093e\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u0902\u092a\u0930\u093e \u0915\u094b \u0906\u091c \u0924\u0915 \u091c\u0940\u0935\u093f\u0924 \u0930\u0916\u0947 \u0939\u0941\u090f \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964<br \/>\n    <\/article>\n<p>    <!-- 4 PEETHAMS GRAND GRID --><\/p>\n<section style=\"padding: 60px 20px; background: #1a1005;\">\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center; color: #D4AF37; font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 50px;\">The Four Amnaya Peethams<\/h2>\n<p>            <!-- EAST - GOVARDHANA --><br \/>\n            <a href=\"https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/puri-peetha\/\" style=\"text-decoration: none;\"><br \/>\n                    <img src=\"https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/swaminischalananda.jpg\" alt=\"Govardhana Peetham - Swami Nischalananda\" style=\"width: 100%; height: 350px; object-fit: cover; display: block; filter: grayscale(20%);\"><br \/>\n                        EAST (Rig Veda)<br \/>\n                        Govardhana Peetham<br \/>\n                        \u0917\u094b\u0935\u0930\u094d\u0927\u0928 \u092e\u0920 (\u092a\u0941\u0930\u0940)<br \/>\n            <\/a><br \/>\n            <!-- SOUTH - SRINGERI --><br \/>\n            <a href=\"https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/sringeri-peetha\/\" style=\"text-decoration: none;\"><br \/>\n                    <img src=\"https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/swamividhushekhar.jpg\" alt=\"Sringeri Peetham - Swami Vidhushekhara\" style=\"width: 100%; height: 350px; object-fit: cover; display: block; filter: grayscale(20%);\"><br \/>\n                        SOUTH (Yajur Veda)<br \/>\n                        Sringeri Peetham<br \/>\n                        \u0936\u094d\u0930\u0943\u0902\u0917\u0947\u0930\u0940 \u0936\u093e\u0930\u0926\u093e \u092a\u0940\u0920<br \/>\n            <\/a><br \/>\n            <!-- WEST - DWARKA --><br \/>\n            <a href=\"https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/dwarka-peetha\/\" style=\"text-decoration: none;\"><br \/>\n                    <img src=\"https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/swamisadananda.jpg\" alt=\"Dwarka Peetham - Swami Sadananda\" style=\"width: 100%; height: 350px; object-fit: cover; display: block; filter: grayscale(20%);\"><br \/>\n                        WEST (Sama Veda)<br \/>\n                        Dwarka Peetham<br \/>\n                        \u0926\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0930\u0915\u093e \u0936\u093e\u0930\u0926\u093e \u092a\u0940\u0920<br \/>\n            <\/a><br \/>\n            <!-- NORTH - JYOTIRMATH --><br \/>\n            <a href=\"https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/jyotishpeetha\/\" style=\"text-decoration: none;\"><br \/>\n                    <img src=\"https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/swamiavimukta.jpg\" alt=\"Jyotirmath - Swami Avimukteshwaranand\" style=\"width: 100%; height: 350px; object-fit: cover; display: block; filter: grayscale(0%);\"><br \/>\n                        NORTH (Atharva Veda)<br \/>\n                        Jyotirmath Peetham<br \/>\n                        \u091c\u094d\u092f\u094b\u0924\u093f\u0930\u094d\u092e\u0920 \u092a\u0940\u0920 (\u092c\u0926\u094d\u0930\u0940\u0928\u093e\u0925)<br \/>\n            <\/a><br \/>\n    <\/section>\n<p><\/body><br \/>\n<\/html><\/p>\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><\/p>\n<!-- \/wp:paragraph -->","post_title":"Aadyaguru Shankaracharya Ji","post_excerpt":"","post_status":"draft","comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","post_password":"","post_name":"adi-shankaracharya","to_ping":"","pinged":"","post_modified":"2026-09-14 11:13:51","post_modified_gmt":"2026-09-14 11:13:51","post_content_filtered":"","post_parent":0,"guid":"https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/?page_id=83","menu_order":0,"post_type":"page","post_mime_type":"","comment_count":"0","url":"https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/?page_id=83"}
